<p>Web excursions brought to you in partnership with <a href="https://fabric.so/?via=brett">Fabric</a>, the best way to organize your notes, tasks, and projects in one place.</p>

<dl>
  <dt><a href="https://tansei.io/">Tansei</a></dt>
  <dd>Tansei is a simple shelf at the edge of your screen for Mac and Windows. Drag anything on, switch apps, pick up where you left off. Private, offline-ready. $7 one-time purchase.</dd>
  <dd>
    <p>In addition to being an excellent clipboard manager, it can take screenshots, pick up colors (that you can copy out in any format), edit and search Markdown notes, and more. A real competitor for Yoink (which is also a great app) and other clipboard managers.</p>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>I gave some feature requests to the developer and they&rsquo;ve already implemented them. Tansei is quickly becoming part of my everyday workflow.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://github.com/juri/tui-fuzzy-finder">juri/tui-fuzzy-finder</a></dt>
  <dd>A fuzzy finder text UI library in Swift, similar to fzf, but for your Swift CLIs. I haven&rsquo;t tested this yet, but bookmarking it for a future project.</dd>
  <dt><a href="https://apps.apple.com/tn/app/groove-number/id6786836303?platform=watch">‎Groove Number App</a></dt>
  <dd>A small utility that tells you how &ldquo;swung&rdquo; a track is, from 50 percent (dead straight) to about 66 percent (full triplet), along with BPM, key, a swing grid and spectrogram, and MIDI export of the groove, all analyzed on the device.</dd>
  <dd>
    <p>A little $1.99 (one-time) utility that &mdash; if you need this kind of thing &mdash; is a great deal.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://pingroom.io/">PingRoom</a></dt>
  <dd>This looks really nice, and I plan to test it out with some teammates this week. You create &ldquo;rooms&rdquo; with invited members and then can ask questions or communicate anything from deploy progress to &ldquo;dinner&rsquo;s ready,&rdquo; with some geofencing, notifications, and integration with your agents. macOS and iOS, free with in-app purchases.</dd>
</dl>

<p>Let Fabric be your second brain, with an all-in-one AI workspace and smart organizer for all your projects, ideas, notes &amp; links. <a href="https://fabric.so/?via=brett">Check it out today.</a></p>

